<</Type/StructElem/S/H4/P 93 0 R/T(Villages Silenced Overnight)/E(Villages Silenced Overnight)/Pg 10 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

109 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H5/P 93 0 R/T(NYOS, CAMEROON \204 On the evening of August 21, 1986, families in the villages around Lake Nyos prepared for another ordinary night. Farmers returned from the fields, herders tied their cattle, and fires burned as meals were cooked. Children drifted to sleep under oil lamps that lit up the highland homes.)/E(NYOS, CAMEROON \204 On the evening of August 21, 1986, families in the villages around Lake Nyos prepared for another ordinary night. Farmers returned from the fields, herders tied their cattle, and fires burned as meals were cooked. Children drifted to sleep under oil lamps that lit up the highland homes.)/Pg 10 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

110 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H5/P 93 0 R/T(At approximately 9:30 p.m., a strange noise echoed from the lake. Witnesses described a deep rumble, lasting no more than thirty seconds. Some thought it was thunder, others said it sounded like rocks tumbling beneath the earth. Then, almost immediately, a white cloud was seen rising from the water\220s surface. The cloud did not rise into the sky like smoke. Instead, it moved downward, clinging to the ground as it spread into valleys and across paths. )/E(At approximately 9:30 p.m., a strange noise echoed from the lake. Witnesses described a deep rumble, lasting no more than thirty seconds. Some thought it was thunder, others said it sounded like rocks tumbling beneath the earth. Then, almost immediately, a white cloud was seen rising from the water\220s surface. The cloud did not rise into the sky like smoke. Instead, it moved downward, clinging to the ground as it spread into valleys and across paths. )/Pg 10 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

111 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 93 0 R/E(9)/Pg 10 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

112 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 93 0 R/E(August 23, 1986)/Pg 10 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj

113 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H5/P 93 0 R/T(Survivors reported that oil lamps extinguished on their own, even with fuel still inside. Livestock stumbled and fell, chickens stopped mid-cluck, and people collapsed suddenly, many unable to make it out of their homes. By dawn, entire villages were silent. Families were found sitting where they had gathered for evening meals, some still holding tools or cups. Bodies were discovered along trails and near cooking fires, suggesting people were )/E(Survivors reported that oil lamps extinguished on their own, even with fuel still inside. Livestock stumbled and fell, chickens stopped mid-cluck, and people collapsed suddenly, many unable to make it out of their homes. By dawn, entire villages were silent. Families were found sitting where they had gathered for evening meals, some still holding tools or cups. Bodies were discovered along trails and near cooking fires, suggesting people were )/Pg 10 0 R/K[11]>>
endobj

114 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H5/P 93 0 R/T(overcome within seconds of noticing the cloud. )/E(overcome within seconds of noticing the cloud. )/Pg 10 0 R/K[12]>>
endobj

115 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H5/P 93 0 R/T(In total, more than 1,700 people died. Thousands of cattle, goats, and other livestock lay lifeless in fields. Even birds had fallen silent, their bodies scattered across the ground. Yet curiously, the land remained untouched. Crops were still upright, houses stood unharmed, and trees bore their leaves.)/E(In total, more than 1,700 people died. Thousands of cattle, goats, and other livestock lay lifeless in fields. Even birds had fallen silent, their bodies scattered across the ground. Yet curiously, the land remained untouched. Crops were still upright, houses stood unharmed, and trees bore their leaves.)/Pg 10 0 R/K[13]>>
endobj

116 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H5/P 93 0 R/T(It was as though life had been erased overnight, leaving the villages intact but empty.)/E(It was as though life had been erased overnight, leaving the villages intact but empty.)/Pg 10 0 R/K[14]>>
endobj

117 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 93 0 R/Pg 10 0 R/A[295 0 R 0]/K[15]>>
endobj

118 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 93 0 R/Pg 10 0 R/A[296 0 R 0]/K[16]>>
endobj

