420 0 obj
<</Title(NYOS, CAMEROON \204 On the evening of August 21, 1986, families in the villages around Lake Nyos prepared for another ordinary night. Farmers returned from the fields, herders tied their cattle, and fires burned as meals were cooked. Children drifted to sleep under oil lamps that lit up the highland homes.)/Dest[10 0 R/Fit]/Parent 388 0 R/Next 421 0 R>>
endobj

421 0 obj
<</Title(At approximately 9:30 p.m., a strange noise echoed from the lake. Witnesses described a deep rumble, lasting no more than thirty seconds. Some thought it was thunder, others said it sounded like rocks tumbling beneath the earth. Then, almost immediately, a white cloud was seen rising from the water\220s surface. The cloud did not rise into the sky like smoke. Instead, it moved downward, clinging to the ground as it spread into valleys and across paths.)/Dest[10 0 R/Fit]/Parent 388 0 R/Prev 420 0 R>>
endobj

