<</Title(In total, more than 1,700 people died. Thousands of cattle, goats, and other livestock lay lifeless in fields. Even birds had fallen silent, their bodies scattered across the ground. Yet curiously, the land remained untouched. Crops were still upright, houses stood unharmed, and trees bore their leaves.)/Dest[10 0 R/Fit]/Parent 422 0 R/Prev 448 0 R/Next 455 0 R>>
